A||||5||Doni Hagan||DIY Lighted mirrors???||||5||
Z||000000||Doni Hagan||07-29-2001||12:59 AM||||A friend just gave me a pair of sun visors with lighted mirrors (from Caddy Cimmaron.) Has anyone ever installed mirrors in a Fiero and, if so, how's it done? I was thinking of just cutting the Caddy visors down, having then re-sewed at the ends and trying to install them that way. IS there a better way?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Doni Hagan||07-29-2001||03:06 PM||||Come on....I KNOW someone out there has done this mod. I'm really anxious to try it and Mrs. Doni would be so appreciative. HELP!! ||||reg||4
Z||000002||8ball2||07-29-2001||03:31 PM||||I have never done it but first you will have to get power to the visor for the lights.<BR>Which would be simple enuf in theory, however to do it right you would have to take your interior apart so as to run power from your dash, to your visor. I would  probably run it from one of the power wires going to the radio such as the constant power and run it behind the molding that is between the door and the windshield(I forget what this is called   post or something) then run the wire under the headliner and have it come out where the visor mounts to the headliner so you can hide the wire and make it look factory. Like I said I have never done this but it is very possible and if takeing your int apart doesn't scare you then should be rather easy.<P>Hope this helps||||reg||1
Z||000003||Philphine||07-29-2001||04:07 PM||||probaly easier still to just power it from the overhead console.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Doni Hagan||07-29-2001||07:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>probaly easier still to just power it from the overhead console.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, that's what I planned on doing. I'm replacing the headliner anyway (just recovered it) so I figured that while I had the interior apart anyway, I'd give the lighted mirrors a shot. Anyone else have any input on this?<P>By the way, DON Y  /  Thanks Buddy...Youve got mail.<P>||||reg||14
Z||000005||Doni Hagan||07-30-2001||02:08 PM||||Okay, here's where I'm at so far. I stripped the Caddy mirrors f the cloth covering. Turns out it's the same material that's in the headliner (in about the same crappy condition.) I removed the "clip" pins from the Fiero visors and, after cutting the Caddy visors down to the same width, crazyglued the pins into place. I will be taking the visors to a local interior shop to have the visors recovered in the same material I re-did the headliner with. At that point, I'll try wiring them into the overhead light console. <P>More to come. ||||reg||14
